{"case_id":"C040","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API entry point","input semantics","state"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["wuffs_base__make_slice_u8_ij","wuffs_base__make_slice_u16_ij","wuffs_base__make_slice_u32_ij","wuffs_base__make_slice_u64_ij","wuffs_base__io_buffer__reader_pointer","wuffs_base__io_buffer__reader_slice","wuffs_base__io_buffer__writer_pointer","wuffs_base__io_buffer__writer_slice","wuffs_private_impl__table_u8__row_u32"],"reason":"S1 changes nine base helpers specifically to handle non-null wrapper objects whose underlying data pointer is NULL. H0 is a JSON-decoder harness driven by input bytes and does not construct null-backed slices, io buffers, or tables with varied indices, lengths, strides, or dimensions. Consequently it does not systematically exercise the changed null-pointer semantics, including cases where metadata is non-zero and prior expressions would perform arithmetic on NULL.","evidence":["The four wuffs_base__make_slice_u*_ij functions now guard ptr before evaluating ptr + i, but H0 never calls these _ij constructors.","wuffs_base__io_buffer__reader_pointer and wuffs_base__io_buffer__reader_slice now require both buf and buf->data.ptr; H0 calls reader_pointer only on its supplied full_src and does not fuzz the io_buffer pointer or its data.ptr and metadata as an API-level state.","wuffs_base__io_buffer__writer_pointer and wuffs_base__io_buffer__writer_slice received the same null-backing guard, but neither function is invoked by H0.","wuffs_private_impl__table_u8__row_u32 now tests t.ptr before computing t.ptr + (t.stride * y), while H0 constructs no wuffs_base__table_u8 values and does not call this row accessor."],"recommended_action":"Add a focused base-API fuzz target that constructs null-backed wuffs_base__slice_* inputs, wuffs_base__io_buffer values, and wuffs_base__table_u8 values with fuzzed indices and metadata, directly invokes every affected helper, and checks that null backing pointers yield NULL pointers or